# Locale directory names Footcream accepts under l10n/.
#
# These are KOReader's OWN codes, because the runtime loads
#   l10n/<gettext current_lang>/foot-cream.mo
# and current_lang is whatever KOReader set. A directory named anything else
# builds and ships a .mo that is never loaded — no error, just an untranslated
# UI. So this list is enforced by builder/build_l10n.sh rather than trusted.
#
# Note the mix: mostly bare language codes, but eleven carry a region
# (af_ZA, bg_BG, en_GB, it_IT, ko_KR, lt_LT, nb_NO, nl_NL, pt_BR, pt_PT,
# ro_MD). Any translation platform must be told this mapping explicitly —
# its default "locale with underscore" would give de_DE where we need de.
#
